1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,419
<i>Want me to get your shoes back? Huh?</i>

2
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:04,421
<i>Get my computers too while you're at it.</i>

3
00:00:04,504 --> 00:00:05,880
<i>Where did they take them?</i>

4
00:00:05,964 --> 00:00:07,549
<i>They said they'll donate them.</i>

5
00:00:07,632 --> 00:00:10,927
<i>B-But where are they giving them away?</i>
<i>We need them!</i>

6
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:11,845
<i>Eric.</i>

7
00:00:11,928 --> 00:00:13,638
<i>You faked your police clearance?</i>

8
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:15,598
<i>This is the original! You have a hit!</i>

9
00:00:15,682 --> 00:00:16,891
<i>Get out!</i>

10
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:18,977
<i>I have to make it up to my kids.</i>

11
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,895
[LUCY] <i>But this is Oliver.</i>

12
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:24,482
<i>We're getting closer to</i>
<i>our meeting with the investors.</i>

13
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:26,860
<i>I think it's too late for that.</i>

14
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:29,446
<i>I know we made the right decision</i>
<i>choosing you.</i>

15
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:31,531
<i>Yes, because the original idea</i>

16
00:00:31,614 --> 00:00:35,076
<i>came from the newest member</i>
<i>of the Pebblng family.</i>

17
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,411
[LINDSAY] <i>Don't let her get away.</i>

18
00:00:38,246 --> 00:00:39,247
[RALPH] <i>Hm? All right!</i>

19
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,000
<i>Can we talk?</i>

20
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:43,668
[YANI] <i>But this isn't right!</i>

21
00:00:43,752 --> 00:00:45,295
<i>Let's just stop this!</i>

22
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:46,713
<i>It's about purpose.</i>

23
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:49,883
<i>And Toni found that purpose</i>
<i>here at LoveList.</i>

24
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:50,842
<i>Toni, make a choice.</i>

25
00:00:50,925 --> 00:00:52,886
<i>Your purpose or me?</i>

26
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:59,976
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

27
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:23,041
It's really unfair that
he's making you choose.

28
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:26,127
Maybe it's about his ego.

29
00:01:27,962 --> 00:01:30,131
You know, if he really loves you…

30
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:33,968
You are working for your future
and your future together.

31
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:36,721
You're working for your life together.

32
00:01:38,056 --> 00:01:40,725
He's so insecure, isn't he?

33
00:01:40,809 --> 00:01:42,852
[TONI] His ego is too strong.

34
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:46,523
He even wanted to show off, didn't he?

35
00:01:47,398 --> 00:01:49,818
He wanted a grand proposal,

36
00:01:49,901 --> 00:01:53,446
so he worked with Valerie, right?

37
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:55,532
He also wanted a big wedding.

38
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:57,117
But how can we even afford that?

39
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:00,703
Are we just going to wait
for his big break?

40
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:03,081
When will that even happen?

41
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:05,416
So let's just break up then!

42
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:08,336
Let's just break up.

43
00:02:08,419 --> 00:02:11,881
If he really wants that,
then I'll give it to him!

44
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:13,049
Calm down.

45
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:15,635
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

46
00:02:15,718 --> 00:02:18,763
I don't mind having a simple wedding.

47
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:21,975
As long as I were marrying him,

48
00:02:22,058 --> 00:02:24,727
I'd be fine with any kind of wedding.

49
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:26,271
But…

50
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:31,192
you also have the right to have
the wedding you've always imagined.

51
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:34,237
[CHARM] It's like a dream come true!

52
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,363
But…

53
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:39,576
the one you'd dream with…

54
00:02:39,659 --> 00:02:40,785
should be…

55
00:02:41,411 --> 00:02:42,871
on the same wavelength as you.

56
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:44,956
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

57
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:46,958
Do you want to file for a leave?

58
00:02:47,917 --> 00:02:49,168
Just take a breath first.

59
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:51,838
- Breathe.
- [TONI SNIFFLES]

60
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:55,216
No need. It's fine.

61
00:02:57,927 --> 00:03:00,179
We're all in this together for LoveList.

62
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:02,015
For friends

63
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:03,349
who are family.

64
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,685
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

65
00:03:05,768 --> 00:03:07,604
For friends…

66
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:10,565
who make boyfriends jealous.

67
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,033
[SIGHS CONTENTEDLY]

68
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:25,872
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

69
00:03:25,955 --> 00:03:27,165
[GUITAR STRUMMING]

70
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:32,253
[SINGING] ♪ <i>I'll hold your hand</i>
<i>In the madness ♪</i>

71
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:37,592
<i>♪ Run to me if they cast you aside ♪</i>

72
00:03:37,675 --> 00:03:40,470
<i>♪ And if you've lost all drive ♪</i>

73
00:03:40,553 --> 00:03:45,683
<i>♪ I'll be your solace ♪</i>

74
00:03:45,767 --> 00:03:50,521
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

75
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:56,861
<i>♪ Let's just dance to</i>
<i>The beat of our hearts ♪</i>

76
00:03:56,945 --> 00:04:00,406
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

77
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:07,163
<i>♪ When you're crying and don't know why ♪</i>

78
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:11,626
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

79
00:04:11,709 --> 00:04:17,257
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

80
00:04:17,924 --> 00:04:24,430
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

81
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:03,970
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

82
00:05:04,053 --> 00:05:06,889
You know, while watching the music video

83
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:08,349
when we were at the bar,

84
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:11,436
I realized that there are
many kinds of love.

85
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:12,478
Heart-pounding.

86
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:13,813
There's also longing.

87
00:05:13,896 --> 00:05:15,815
And love full sacrifices.

88
00:05:15,898 --> 00:05:17,066
[BILLY] Yes.

89
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:20,820
But all of them are magical
in their own way.

90
00:05:20,903 --> 00:05:22,989
I also remember what you said, Charm,

91
00:05:23,072 --> 00:05:26,659
that we all deserve to have that wedding
we've always dreamed of.

92
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:29,245
A dream come true.

93
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:30,455
Yes.

94
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:32,832
Because a wedding is not just an event.

95
00:05:32,915 --> 00:05:36,711
It's a celebration of love
you've waited for.

96
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:38,087
Fought for.

97
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:41,007
Chief, I think I know where you're going.

98
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:44,427
[MARJ] We will make
the LoveListers' wedding

99
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:46,679
a once-in-a-lifetime experience.

100
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:50,266
Yes, because we are
not just a dating platform

101
00:05:50,349 --> 00:05:52,310
that sees couples as profiles.

102
00:05:52,393 --> 00:05:56,939
We celebrate the unique love story
behind each one.

103
00:05:57,023 --> 00:06:01,486
We will give a package
that transforms the entire wedding,

104
00:06:01,569 --> 00:06:03,237
from the ceremony

105
00:06:03,321 --> 00:06:04,739
to the reception,

106
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:06,741
into a story unfolding.

107
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:10,036
We'll have different themes,
depending on what the couple wants,

108
00:06:10,119 --> 00:06:13,831
while still honoring
the true essence of a wedding.

109
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:18,086
Me, I've always wanted a beach wedding.

110
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:20,171
Okay. You want a beach wedding?

111
00:06:20,254 --> 00:06:23,424
Then the ceremony happens by the shore.

112
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:27,095
Soft, golden sunset lighting.

113
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:29,347
Surfboards. Coral reefs.

114
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:31,224
Tropical arrangements.

115
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:32,725
And your reception?

116
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:35,603
Floating reefs. Coastal-inspired cuisine.

117
00:06:35,686 --> 00:06:39,440
Live performances that feel
like a seaside festival.

118
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:42,568
You want a Hollywood
movie-inspired wedding?

119
00:06:42,652 --> 00:06:46,155
Then the ceremony starts
with a red carpet.

120
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:49,033
Then the orchestra will play
movie soundtracks.

121
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:50,451
Cinematic lighting.

122
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:54,705
And then, the wedding invitations
will look like movie-inspired tickets.

123
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:57,792
How great!

124
00:06:57,875 --> 00:07:00,670
[TONI] This is not just
a wedding you attend.

125
00:07:00,753 --> 00:07:03,339
It is a wedding that you watch,

126
00:07:03,422 --> 00:07:04,549
you feel,

127
00:07:04,632 --> 00:07:06,217
you remember forever.

128
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,969
- Yes.
- My gosh!

129
00:07:08,052 --> 00:07:09,679
I'm about to cry out of excitement.

130
00:07:09,762 --> 00:07:11,055
Imagine the hype!

131
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:12,765
The views.

132
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:15,476
The brands and the sponsors!

133
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,562
Wait, but the question now is,

134
00:07:17,645 --> 00:07:20,982
who is the couple that
we're going to feature?

135
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:22,650
[GRUNTS AGREEMENT]

136
00:07:22,733 --> 00:07:25,611
No, no, no, no, no, the real question is,

137
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:28,030
how do we fund that?

138
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:30,908
[DOOR SQUEAKING]

139
00:07:32,869 --> 00:07:37,999
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

140
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:41,836
[MOUTHS SILENTLY]

141
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:43,171
I'm…

142
00:07:43,254 --> 00:07:44,422
I'm willing to commit.

143
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:49,594
[RALPH] Yeah.

144
00:07:49,677 --> 00:07:51,429
I'll invest.

145
00:07:53,389 --> 00:08:00,396
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

146
00:08:02,106 --> 00:08:03,191
Dude!

147
00:08:03,941 --> 00:08:05,735
[BILLY] Why haven't you gone home yet?

148
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:08,404
It's okay now.

149
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:10,823
[JORDAN] We can still use these old PCs.

150
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:12,533
We don't need to replace them yet.

151
00:08:12,617 --> 00:08:13,493
[BILLY] Wow!

152
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:15,328
Oh, very good!

153
00:08:15,411 --> 00:08:17,079
Very good, thank you.

154
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:18,039
Very good.

155
00:08:18,122 --> 00:08:20,166
My gosh, how sticky!

156
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:22,877
You're so sweaty!
Why didn't you turn on the AC?

157
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:23,878
Really, huh?

158
00:08:23,961 --> 00:08:25,546
You stink already.

159
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:27,173
- Smell it.
- No way!

160
00:08:27,256 --> 00:08:28,966
- Go ahead. Smell it.
- What are you doing?

161
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,343
What is this?

162
00:08:30,426 --> 00:08:32,553
- Oh, I really do smell.
- [BILLY] Wait.

163
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:34,263
<i>As you come home</i>

164
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:37,225
- Wait--
<i>- I feel the weight</i>

165
00:08:37,308 --> 00:08:39,268
<i>Even if you don't say it</i>

166
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:40,728
<i>With your lips</i>

167
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:43,314
<i>Just stay here</i>

168
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,858
<i>Beside me</i>

169
00:08:46,817 --> 00:08:48,319
It's not yet done.

170
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:50,863
It's beautiful.

171
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,865
This love song is really good.

172
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:54,825
It's not finished yet.
And it's not a love song.

173
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:55,910
What is it then?

174
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:57,119
It's a

175
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:58,329
friendship song.

176
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:00,289
Mm…?

177
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:04,377
I'm glad you started writing again.

178
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:06,546
Do you remember when
we were in high school?

179
00:09:06,629 --> 00:09:08,422
You serenaded a girl.

180
00:09:08,506 --> 00:09:10,341
What was her name again?

181
00:09:10,424 --> 00:09:12,343
- It's Jelou!
- Jelou.

182
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:14,762
- But you were rejected.
- But I was rejected.

183
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:16,806
- Wow.
- Yup.

184
00:09:16,889 --> 00:09:19,600
But if you serenaded someone
with that song,

185
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:21,727
I feel like you'd have a chance.

186
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:23,020
It's good!

187
00:09:23,104 --> 00:09:25,106
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

188
00:09:25,189 --> 00:09:27,775
[OPERATOR 1]
You should probably circle back to why,

189
00:09:27,858 --> 00:09:30,111
try and see if it works for you.

190
00:09:30,194 --> 00:09:31,320
If it doesn't…

191
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:32,321
[BILLY] Sorry, Hiraya.

192
00:09:32,405 --> 00:09:33,447
Where's Cristy?

193
00:09:33,531 --> 00:09:34,865
She worked under time, Ms. Billy.

194
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:36,200
Her baby got sick.

195
00:09:36,284 --> 00:09:37,868
Ah, okay. Thank you.

196
00:09:37,952 --> 00:09:44,709
[RINGING]

197
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:49,255
Hi, good evening.

198
00:09:49,338 --> 00:09:50,881
Thank you for calling LoveLine,

199
00:09:50,965 --> 00:09:54,051
your safe space for honest,
heart-to-heart conversations.

200
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:55,678
How can I support you today?

201
00:09:55,761 --> 00:09:57,263
Hi.

202
00:09:57,346 --> 00:09:58,556
I'm Melissa.

203
00:09:58,639 --> 00:09:59,890
[MELISSA] <i>I'm…</i>

204
00:09:59,974 --> 00:10:02,393
having second thoughts about my wedding.

205
00:10:02,977 --> 00:10:04,145
Can you tell me more?

206
00:10:04,228 --> 00:10:06,022
Only if you're comfortable.

207
00:10:06,105 --> 00:10:07,898
I'm here to listen.

208
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:09,108
Thanks, Billy.

209
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:11,319
Um…

210
00:10:11,402 --> 00:10:12,820
[GIGGLES FAINTLY]

211
00:10:12,903 --> 00:10:14,363
I love Theo, you know.

212
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:16,365
We're a perfect match.

213
00:10:16,449 --> 00:10:19,869
[MELISSA] <i>Actually,</i>
<i>we're a 94% match on LoveList.</i>

214
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:20,995
<i>But there's just one problem.</i>

215
00:10:21,078 --> 00:10:22,663
My dad doesn't approve of him.

216
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:24,707
May I ask why?

217
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,667
You know, Theo is diligent.

218
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:27,668
He's hardworking.

219
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:29,378
[MELISSA] <i>He's good at what he does.</i>

220
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:31,547
But my dad still sees him

221
00:10:32,548 --> 00:10:33,549
as a failure.

222
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:35,676
That sounds painful to hear,

223
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:37,928
especially when it comes
from someone you love.

224
00:10:38,012 --> 00:10:40,348
[BILLY] <i>Did something happen before</i>

225
00:10:40,431 --> 00:10:42,892
that made your father feel that way
towards Theo?

226
00:10:42,975 --> 00:10:45,728
[MELISSA] <i>He doesn't like Theo's job.</i>

227
00:10:45,811 --> 00:10:47,521
He's just a cook.

228
00:10:47,605 --> 00:10:50,399
Your dad may not be expressing it well,

229
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:52,860
but I think

230
00:10:52,943 --> 00:10:54,737
he just wants to protect you.

231
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:56,155
You know, sometimes,

232
00:10:56,238 --> 00:10:59,116
even love can come out as control.

233
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,743
What matters is

234
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:03,329
how you feel when you are together.

235
00:11:03,412 --> 00:11:05,331
Do you feel safe?

236
00:11:05,414 --> 00:11:06,540
Supported?

237
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:07,667
Seen?

238
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,210
Yes, I do.

239
00:11:09,293 --> 00:11:11,462
That's what matters the most, Melissa.

240
00:11:11,545 --> 00:11:13,297
Because the life you're building

241
00:11:13,381 --> 00:11:16,258
isn't measured by job titles or money,

242
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:18,094
but by how you treat each other,

243
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:19,970
especially when it's just the two of you.

244
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:22,181
But what if my dad never accepts him?

245
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:24,058
I know that's scary,

246
00:11:24,141 --> 00:11:28,854
especially if you want the people you love
to love each other too.

247
00:11:28,938 --> 00:11:31,649
But you know what's most important?

248
00:11:31,732 --> 00:11:34,318
What matters most is your happiness,

249
00:11:34,402 --> 00:11:36,070
especially when it comes to your family.

250
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:43,160
And your marriage is about your happiness.
So follow your heart.

251
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:45,037
As for Theo,

252
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:47,248
he has to prove himself.

253
00:11:47,331 --> 00:11:48,999
<i>Because you have to remember,</i>

254
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:51,877
marriage isn't just about
two people in love.

255
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:55,756
It's a union of families.

256
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,967
Thank you for calling LoveLine, Melissa.

257
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,510
I hope you feel better.

258
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:03,973
[HEADSET CLACKS SOFTLY]

259
00:12:04,056 --> 00:12:07,643
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:11,188
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

261
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:12,898
- [UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]
- [RYTHMIC CLAPPING]

262
00:12:12,982 --> 00:12:14,650
[INSTRUCTOR] One, two, three, go!

263
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:17,653
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

264
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:23,159
[INSTRUCTOR COUNTING INDISTINCTLY]

265
00:12:30,875 --> 00:12:34,462
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

266
00:12:34,545 --> 00:12:36,380
Who says you're the only one?

267
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:38,048
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

268
00:12:39,842 --> 00:12:41,510
Wow.

269
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:43,929
[INSTRUCTOR] Six, seven, eight…

270
00:12:45,723 --> 00:12:47,558
- We made it.
- [LYDIA] Hello!

271
00:12:47,641 --> 00:12:49,226
- Hi, Billy.
- Hi, Auntie Pres.

272
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:51,312
- [LYDIA] Hi!
- Our singer.

273
00:12:51,395 --> 00:12:52,646
[PRECIOUS] Wow!

274
00:12:54,106 --> 00:12:55,733
[ABI] Here, Ms. Cams!

275
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:59,820
Pebblng will be covering
everything the couple will wear.

276
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:03,449
Um, from the wedding ceremony
all the way to the reception.

277
00:13:03,532 --> 00:13:05,659
The grand wedding gown, the groom's suit,

278
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:07,453
even the entourage's outfits.

279
00:13:07,536 --> 00:13:08,913
Pebblng will take care of all of it.

280
00:13:08,996 --> 00:13:10,915
They won't have to worry about a thing.

281
00:13:10,998 --> 00:13:13,209
We've also secured a sponsor for the food.

282
00:13:13,292 --> 00:13:15,169
And someone will be covering
the event as well.

283
00:13:15,252 --> 00:13:16,295
This is it?

284
00:13:17,379 --> 00:13:19,507
This is so bland!

285
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:21,383
How can we enhance this?

286
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:24,762
Well, LoveFeast's first couple
is kind of basic.

287
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:27,431
Both in their late twenties.

288
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:28,599
Corporate employees.

289
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:30,059
Nothing too special.

290
00:13:30,142 --> 00:13:33,229
So you're saying we settle
for mediocre, is that it?

291
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:36,982
Abi, ideas, please.

292
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:38,651
Uh, ideas…

293
00:13:38,734 --> 00:13:40,194
Uh, okay!

294
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:42,238
Ah!

295
00:13:42,321 --> 00:13:45,908
Ms. Cams, what if we make the theme

296
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:49,286
match the couple's personalities?

297
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:50,204
Mh-mm.

298
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:53,207
They're both in their late twenties
and work corporate jobs.

299
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:55,626
The guy works in a BPO,

300
00:13:56,627 --> 00:13:58,963
while the girl is an office administrator…

301
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:03,384
and they met on Pebblng!

302
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:04,468
Yes!

303
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:07,763
Abi, I saw this great idea.

304
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:10,224
A city love story.

305
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:11,559
Perfect!

306
00:14:11,642 --> 00:14:13,477
A city love story.

307
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:15,688
Imagine this, Ms. Cams.

308
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:18,440
Um… in the middle of a busy city,

309
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:21,110
our couple meets.

310
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:24,321
Their prenup shoot
features the city skyline.

311
00:14:24,405 --> 00:14:27,616
The whole vibe is,

312
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:30,828
"We found love in a hopeless place."

313
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:32,872
You know, like the song!

314
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:39,295
Just imagine it, in the middle of traffic,
in a loud and chaotic world,

315
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:44,133
they found each other.

316
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:47,261
Okay, that's great for the prenup.

317
00:14:47,344 --> 00:14:50,723
But remember, we have to think
about the entire event.

318
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:52,850
Besides, we might run out of time.

319
00:14:52,933 --> 00:14:54,435
Abi, is it approved?

320
00:14:54,518 --> 00:14:56,395
- Oh, shut up.
- What?!

321
00:14:56,478 --> 00:15:00,566
I'm just saying our timeline
is based on the original plan.

322
00:15:00,649 --> 00:15:04,028
Exactly! Yes, Morrie, you're right
about that. I agree with you.

323
00:15:04,111 --> 00:15:05,905
Morrie's right, Ms. Cams.

324
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:10,993
We need to get started now
before LoveList steals our idea.

325
00:15:11,076 --> 00:15:14,246
Especially now that they're
already falling behind.

326
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:18,250
Are we really going to let them
make a comeback, Ms. Cams?

327
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:21,253
Aggressive. I like it.

328
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:23,047
Okay, meeting adjourned.

329
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:24,381
Morrie, let's go. Next meeting.

330
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:26,467
But, Abi, give me more.

331
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:27,718
More!

332
00:15:27,801 --> 00:15:30,137
- I like that idea, so give me more.
- Sure, Ms. Cams.

333
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:31,972
[CAMILLE] Morrie!

334
00:15:36,393 --> 00:15:37,686
[PHONE RINGING]

335
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:43,108
[RINGING CONTINUES]

336
00:15:44,818 --> 00:15:46,487
[LINE RINGING]

337
00:15:47,696 --> 00:15:49,281
[LINE RINGING]

338
00:15:51,533 --> 00:15:52,493
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

339
00:15:52,576 --> 00:15:53,452
[PHONE CHIMES]

340
00:15:53,535 --> 00:15:58,248
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

341
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,211
Caloy!

342
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:06,048
[CALOY] 'Bi, I missed you.
Did you get butterflies?

343
00:16:06,131 --> 00:16:08,175
Seriously, Caloy?!
I don't have time for your nonsense.

344
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:10,094
- What are you doing here?
- Don't you appreciate me?

345
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:11,011
Come here. Hurry up!

346
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:12,846
So you finally admit
you've forgotten about me.

347
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:15,474
Caloy, what is your problem?!
What are you talking about?!

348
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:16,767
Seriously?!

349
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:18,811
Can't you see I'm working?

350
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:20,229
You're starting to sound like my mom,

351
00:16:20,312 --> 00:16:22,398
always asking where I'm going
and what I'm doing!

352
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:25,526
I wouldn't even be surprised
if she showed up here and caused a scene.

353
00:16:25,609 --> 00:16:26,777
That will totally ruin my plan.

354
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:27,903
Just like you!

355
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,279
What, are you my mother now?!

356
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:30,280
No!

357
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:32,491
Then why are you here?!

358
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:36,870
So what am I to you, anyway?

359
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:41,291
- Because I love you.
- Cut it out!

360
00:16:43,585 --> 00:16:44,712
Fine, I will.

361
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:47,923
So what's the update on your computers?

362
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:50,175
[SCOFFS] I don't care about that anymore!

363
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:51,885
They're gone,
and I'm never getting them back.

364
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:56,223
What's important is figuring out
how to get back at that woman.

365
00:16:57,808 --> 00:17:00,102
And you, you've been bugging me
since the other night.

366
00:17:00,185 --> 00:17:02,980
You just won't let it go.
Why do you even care about the computers?

367
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:04,064
'Bi, I'm sorry.

368
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:06,650
Uh…

369
00:17:07,901 --> 00:17:09,653
Nobody's going to see it anyway, right?

370
00:17:10,279 --> 00:17:11,739
It must have been deleted.

371
00:17:11,822 --> 00:17:12,948
See what?

372
00:17:14,616 --> 00:17:16,326
One of the computers

373
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,912
has our pictures and videos on it.

374
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:20,372
Remember your birthday?

375
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:22,124
When we were doing karaoke?

376
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:23,917
[HUFFS] What are you talking about?

377
00:17:24,001 --> 00:17:26,086
You were drunk, and you looked so cute.

378
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:28,380
So I took videos of you.

379
00:17:28,464 --> 00:17:31,467
[EXHALES]
So why is it on the computer?

380
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:33,510
I was editing a video.

381
00:17:33,594 --> 00:17:35,220
It was supposed to be your birthday gift.

382
00:17:35,304 --> 00:17:36,889
Sorry, it completely slipped my mind.

383
00:17:37,806 --> 00:17:39,433
- Ow!
- Seriously, Caloy?!

384
00:17:40,309 --> 00:17:41,560
Find that computer, okay?

385
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:43,687
Every single picture and video
on it has to be deleted!

386
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:48,025
You know no one can ever find out
that we're connected!

387
00:17:48,108 --> 00:17:49,568
Where are they donating them?

388
00:17:49,651 --> 00:17:56,241
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

389
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:58,994
I only know of one place
they'd donate them to.

390
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:06,168
Thanks again for volunteering.

391
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:08,087
Anytime. It's for them.

392
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:10,255
Go eat first.

393
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:14,176
Uh, I still have another
session at the gym.

394
00:18:14,259 --> 00:18:15,385
- That's too bad.
- Uh…

395
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:16,887
- Maybe next time.
- Sure, sure.

396
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:19,515
Oh, wait. Billy, Jordan!

397
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:21,558
- [BILLY] Uh, excuse me.
- [WOMAN] Oh, sure.

398
00:18:23,602 --> 00:18:24,895
- [BILLY] Hmm?
- Yes!

399
00:18:24,978 --> 00:18:27,898
Billy, Jordan, this is Brandon.

400
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:29,483
- Ah!
- Yes, yes.

401
00:18:29,566 --> 00:18:30,984
- Hello!
- [BRANDON] Hello!

402
00:18:31,068 --> 00:18:32,778
- Jordan.
- Hello, Jordan.

403
00:18:32,861 --> 00:18:34,196
Billy. Nice to meet you.

404
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:35,656
Nice to meet you too…

405
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:36,782
- Jo--I mean, Billy!
- Mh-mm.

406
00:18:36,865 --> 00:18:37,991
- Billy!
- Billy!

407
00:18:38,075 --> 00:18:39,076
- Jordan.
- Oh!

408
00:18:39,159 --> 00:18:41,453
Your Auntie Pres talks
about you all the time.

409
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:43,247
- Oh, really?
- She's so proud of you.

410
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:45,040
- [CHUCKLES]
- Ah…

411
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:48,460
You know, she talks about
you a lot too--[CHUCKLES]

412
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:49,795
- I'm just kidding.
- Oh, all right…

413
00:18:49,878 --> 00:18:51,338
I'd better get going.

414
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:54,133
Nice to meet you again, Jordan, Billy.

415
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:55,759
- Yes!
- Uh, bye.

416
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:57,719
- Take care.
- Bye!

417
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:00,264
- Oh, you!
- Hmm, hmm.

418
00:19:00,347 --> 00:19:02,266
He seems nice, right?

419
00:19:02,349 --> 00:19:04,351
- Don't you think?
- So, how have you been?

420
00:19:04,434 --> 00:19:05,727
I want my own Brandon too.

421
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,229
- Hmm!
- Oh!

422
00:19:07,312 --> 00:19:09,148
So, how's LoveList doing?

423
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:10,566
We've just been a little busy, Auntie.

424
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:13,610
But stay tuned.
We have a lot of new things coming.

425
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:16,071
- I'll look forward to it.
- [CHUCKLING]

426
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:18,282
Sorry it's taken us so long to come back.

427
00:19:18,365 --> 00:19:21,118
That's okay. I know you've been busy.

428
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:23,787
Thanks for donating those computers.

429
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,414
- And…
- Thank you!

430
00:19:25,497 --> 00:19:28,792
Nice work convincing Jordan
to perform here.

431
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:30,502
- He can't say no to you.
- All it took was food.

432
00:19:30,586 --> 00:19:32,462
It's my pleasure, Auntie Pres.

433
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:35,465
[GUITAR STRUMMING]

434
00:19:35,549 --> 00:19:38,844
[SINGING]<i> ♪ Just take a deep breath ♪</i>

435
00:19:38,927 --> 00:19:42,347
<i>♪ And don't force it anymore ♪</i>

436
00:19:42,431 --> 00:19:45,142
<i>♪ Just give yourself ♪</i>

437
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,436
<i>♪ Some time alone ♪</i>

438
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:52,316
<i>♪ We don't have anything ♪</i>

439
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:55,903
<i>♪ Left to prove ♪</i>

440
00:19:55,986 --> 00:19:57,738
<i>♪ After everything ♪</i>

441
00:19:57,821 --> 00:20:01,533
<i>♪ We've been through, right? ♪</i>

442
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:08,373
<i>♪ Even in the silence ♪</i>

443
00:20:08,457 --> 00:20:15,130
<i>♪ You're the only one on my mind ♪</i>

444
00:20:16,715 --> 00:20:21,762
<i>♪ Even in the silence ♪</i>

445
00:20:21,845 --> 00:20:28,560
<i>♪ You're the only one on my mind ♪</i>

446
00:20:29,144 --> 00:20:34,149
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

447
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,275
[GROANS]

448
00:20:49,539 --> 00:20:56,463
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

449
00:21:11,311 --> 00:21:18,318
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

450
00:21:33,208 --> 00:21:40,173
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

451
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:47,431
[OLIVER] <i>I also want my parents</i>
<i>to be proud of me.</i>

452
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:49,641
<i>And that's my inspiration</i>
<i>to study harder.</i>

453
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:52,436
<i>Sometimes, I imagine them</i>
<i>looking down on me from heaven.</i>

454
00:21:52,519 --> 00:21:53,979
[ZANDRO] <i>When are you</i>
<i>going to pay me?</i>

455
00:21:54,062 --> 00:21:55,397
[ENRICO YELPS] <i>Oliver!</i>

456
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:57,607
[ABI] <i>Every single picture and video</i>
<i>on it has to be deleted!</i>

457
00:21:57,691 --> 00:21:59,484
[MARIELA] <i>This is where Bea goes!</i>

458
00:22:00,152 --> 00:22:02,279
<i>- Don't be too loud.</i>
<i>- Just tell me the truth!</i>

459
00:22:02,362 --> 00:22:03,405
<i>I am telling the truth.</i>

460
00:22:03,488 --> 00:22:06,033
[STAFF] <i>Ms. Mariela is acting out.</i>
<i>She's hurting someone.</i>

461
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:07,284
[BILLY] <i>Caloy?</i>

462
00:22:07,367 --> 00:22:08,577
<i>Where are you going?!</i>

463
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:10,120
[GRUNTING, GROANING]

464
00:22:10,203 --> 00:22:11,955
- [BOTH GRUNTING]
<i>- Come on, hit me!</i>

465
00:22:12,039 --> 00:22:13,832
- [MORRIE] <i>In deep thought, huh?</i>
- [LINE RINGING]

466
00:22:15,042 --> 00:22:18,670
<i>He's taking my daughter away from me.</i>
<i>I can't let that happen.</i>

467
00:22:18,754 --> 00:22:20,255
<i>Who is your daughter?</i>

468
00:22:20,339 --> 00:22:22,424
<i>Her name is Bea.</i>

469
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:26,636
<i>Don't ever talk to Billy again.</i>

470
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:28,930
<i>I thought she was your idol.</i>

471
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:30,766
<i>Her niceness is all just an act.</i>

472
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:33,310
<i>Don't let her fool you.</i>

473
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:34,770
<i>She's so cunning!</i>

474
00:22:34,853 --> 00:22:38,565
[PRECIOUS] <i>I bet Caloy's trying</i>
<i>to steal our computers.</i>

475
00:22:38,648 --> 00:22:40,734
<i>These computers came from Abi.</i>

476
00:22:40,817 --> 00:22:42,944
<i>I think he needed something from here.</i>
